{"author":{"id":"a66e0db0201c515c5090d5e52c036411dda9ba2f138110a926616a18a8ea0dd6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790971320,"nonce":"jC+2vy1zj8xbBRlF+LHE4tCPd40=","title":"the web backend implements 93 of the API's 237 natives","message":"crates/xgpu-backend/src/template/web.rs defines 93 of the 237 `#[native]` functions api/gpu.api.rs declares. A program in a browser that calls any of the other 144 gets \"`\u003cnative\u003e` is not available on the web\", thrown when it reaches the call. hlwgpu's browser bundle (xgpu.wasm) ships with this gap, and so does any Caribou web build over xgpu.\n\nFound 2026-10-02 by running a triangle through xwindow and xgpu in Ash's page in headless Chrome (Ash d19312b41993d0b2bf909d76f28d40783c4cf869, local). Three gaps stopped it. The working tree now covers them, and the triangle draws at vsync:\n\n- `GpuRequestAdapterOptions.compatibleSurface` rejected the adapter request. Every WebGPU adapter presents to the page's canvas, the only surface there is, so the option is now accepted and has no effect.\n- `surface_capabilities` and the `capabilities_*` getters now answer what WebGPU allows a canvas. Formats: the preferred one, then bgra8unorm, rgba8unorm and rgba16float. Present mode: Fifo. Alpha modes: Opaque and PreMultiplied. Usages: COPY_SRC | COPY_DST | TEXTURE_BINDING | RENDER_ATTACHMENT.\n- `adapter_name` reads GPUAdapterInfo: its description, else its device, else its vendor and architecture. Chrome gives \"apple metal-3\". `adapter_backend` returns BrowserWebGpu, and the subgroup sizes come from GPUAdapterInfo.\n\nStill missing, with a WebGPU counterpart to forward to:\n\n- resources: sampler_create, sampler_destroy, bind_group_layout_create, pipeline_layout_create, pipeline_layout_destroy, bindings_sampler, bindings_view, query_set_create, query_set_count, query_set_type, query_set_destroy, and the texture getters (texture_width, texture_height, texture_depth_or_array_layers, texture_mip_level_count, texture_sample_count, texture_get_dimension, texture_get_format, texture_usage);\n- uploads and copies: queue_write_texture(_with), buffer_copy_in, encoder_copy_buffer_to_texture(_with), encoder_copy_texture_to_buffer(_with), encoder_copy_texture_to_texture(_with), encoder_clear_buffer, encoder_resolve_query_set;\n- passes: render_pass_begin_with, compute_pass_begin_with, pass_reset, render_set_viewport, render_set_scissor_rect, render_set_blend_constant, render_set_stencil_reference, render_set_bind_group_offsets, compute_set_bind_group_offsets, render_set_vertex_buffer_range, render_set_index_buffer_range, render_draw_range, render_draw_indexed_range, render_draw_indirect, render_draw_indexed_indirect, compute_dispatch_indirect, encoder_compute_indirect, render_begin_occlusion_query, render_end_occlusion_query, encoder_insert_debug_marker, encoder_push_debug_group, encoder_pop_debug_group;\n- render bundles: bundle_* (13) and render_execute_bundle;\n- asynchronous pipelines: render_pipeline_create_async, compute_pipeline_create_async;\n- shader diagnostics: shader_compilation_info, shader_messages, compilation_* (8);\n- errors and loss: error_scope_push, error_scope_pop, error_filter, error_message, error_destroy, device_take_error, device_lost, lost_message, lost_reason, lost_destroy;\n- features and limits: adapter_feature, adapter_limit, device_feature, device_limit;\n- queue_timestamp_period, which is always 1 (WebGPU timestamps are nanoseconds);\n- instance_create_with, whose options choose native backends; the web could ignore them, as it now does compatibleSurface.\n\nWithout a WebGPU counterpart, which wgpu adds; raising for these is right:\n\n- adapter identity: adapter_vendor_id, adapter_device_id, adapter_device_type, adapter_driver, adapter_driver_info, adapter_pci_bus_id, adapter_pipeline_cache_key, adapter_format_features, adapter_format_usages, adapter_native_feature, adapter_native_limit, device_native_feature, device_native_limit;\n- ray tracing: blas_* (4), tlas_* (5), queue_compact_blas, encoder_build_acceleration_structures;\n- mesh shaders and multi-draw: mesh_pipeline_create(_async), render_draw_mesh_tasks(_indirect), render_multi_draw_* (6);\n- immediates, statistics and in-pass timestamps: compute_set_immediates, render_set_immediates, compute_begin/end_pipeline_statistics, render_begin/end_pipeline_statistics, compute_write_timestamp, render_write_timestamp, encoder_write_timestamp;\n- pipeline caches (pipeline_cache_* (3)), shader_create_passthrough, encoder_clear_texture, external_texture_create and external_texture_destroy (a page's video frames, which a program cannot name).\n\nTo find the gap again: compare the `#[native(...)]` names in api/gpu.api.rs with the `pub fn` names in the web template.","files":null}]}